Hi,

ever since upgrading to 2.6.x I've been having problems with acpi in the sense 
that's not really working. it's much better than letting everything for apm 
to do as my processor was almost in flames and the fan wouldn't start.
Now the most annoying thing: the fan doesn't start until the temerature goes 
above 85 so I start the machine, wait until it gets hot and then restart, 
otherwise it would shut down on it's own. After starting, the fan won't stop 
and the processor stabilizes at about 60.
I'm with a 2.6.5, I installed the patch for reading the dsdt from initrd and I 
tried fixing (just a couple of removed stars *) the original dsdt and I'm 
left with seven times the warning:
"Not all control paths return a value (_DIS)"
I also tried the dsdt in the database even though it's for a different 
machine, but it seems to be the same configuration. The fan still doesn't 
stop and the next suspect is the C2 state the processor is in. How exactly do 
I take that out of processor.c and what othe suggestions do you have?


I'm just gonna attach the dsdt I tryied to fix.
Thanks a lot,
Cristian
